{
  "dom_id": "step-q68547",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "A pack contains $24$ fluid ounce of cream cheese and costs $$6.00.$ What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$  \n\n$$\n24÷8=3\n$$\n\nSo, $24$ fluid ounces is the same as $3$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $3:$ \n\n$$\n6.00÷3=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cream cheese costs $$2.00$ per cup.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
